# libcat89

A small, representation-neutral generic category-theory library for strict
ISO C89. It models a category directly as

    (Ob, Mor, dom, cod, id, compose)

and layers derived categorical structures above that kernel. The category
core carries no assumption about finiteness, enumerability, decidable equality,
executable morphisms, canonical forms, or any derived structure. Laws are
contracts promised by backends; optional checkers verify them when the required
capabilities exist.

## Design in one line

    minimal category core
    + strictly layered categorical structures
    + orthogonal computational capabilities (equality, enumeration)

## Public layout

Nested headers under `include/cat89/`:

- `status.h`, `alloc.h`, `core.h` — the category kernel.
- `eq.h`, `enum.h` — orthogonal capabilities.
- `functor.h`, `nat.h` — 1-categorical algebra.
- `iso.h`, `split.h` — derived structures wrapping ordinary morphisms (CAT-I3).
- `check.h` — explicit law checking, including the exhaustive library sweeps.
- `diagram.h`, `cone.h`, `limit.h` — diagrams, cones/cocones, limits/colimits.
- `shape.h`, `find.h`, `findlim.h` — finite shape categories and the
  terminal/initial + binary-product/coproduct, equalizer/coequalizer, and
  pullback/pushout finders.
- `opposite.h` — generic category construction (reverses arrows).
- `product.h`, `comma.h`, `arrow.h`, `slice.h`, `coslice.h` — generic wrapper
  categories (pairs, spans, commutative squares, triangles).
- `finite.h`, `free.h`, `thin.h` — concrete reference backends.
- `cat89.h` — umbrella header.

`core.h` never includes a higher-level header (enforced by the architecture
gate).

## Implemented and green

Each module below passes the workspace `green` matrix (strict C89∩C23 under
GCC and Clang, clang-tidy, canonical Allman format) and has unit tests:

- category kernel (`status`/`alloc`/`core`)
- equality + enumeration capabilities
- finite backend (builder, immutable store, category/eq/enumeration)
- free (path) and thin (preorder) backends
- functor, natural transformation (core, vertical/whisker/horizontal), iso,
  split mono/epi
- local law checkers and the **exhaustive category-law checker**
  (`cat89_check_category_exhaustive`, identity + associativity over an
  enumerated finite ambient)
- **exhaustive derived law-family sweeps** (W5): iso, split mono/epi, functor
  (identity + composition), naturality, and cone/cocone commutation cells, each
  counting into a `cat89_check_result` and refusing with `CAT89_NOT_SUPPORTED`
  when a required capability is absent
- opposite-category construction
- generic wrapper categories: product, comma (over functors), arrow, slice,
  coslice
- shape categories (`shape.h`) and terminal/initial object finders (`find.h`)
- **finite universal-construction finders** (`findlim.h`, W4.2): binary
  product/coproduct, equalizer/coequalizer, and pullback/pushout, each returning
  a genuine `cat89_limit`/`cat89_colimit` over the relevant shape diagram whose
  cone/cocone carries a working universal `factor` (CAT-I9). Decoy apices are
  never substituted for the genuine apex.
- hardening (W6): mock-backend observer/context split, an allocator-failure
  campaign across the finite builder, shape, every wrapper/derived constructor,
  and the finders (error-atomic under injected single-allocation failure), a
  mock callback-failure matrix confirming verbatim status propagation, and a
  clean `just sanitize` (ASan+UBSan+LSan) over the whole suite
- ABI/architecture audit gates (W7): core-header isolation, header include-graph
  acyclicity, exported-symbol inventory, and struct-exposure review
- correctness closure: mandatory `owns_obj`/`owns_mor` provenance enforced by
  every raw-handle API; representation-independent object identity; one-pass
  finder enumeration; failure-atomic finite builder with full validation;
  checked size/refcount arithmetic; unambiguous factor cardinality

## Build and test

    just build        # strict C89, archive build/libcat89.a (src objects only)
    just smoke        # one end-to-end path first
    just unit         # per-concern unit programs
    just test         # smoke then unit
    just headers      # each public header compiles standalone
    just green        # sibling green toolchain matrix
    just arch         # ABI/architecture hygiene gates (also run by lint)
    just sanitize     # whole suite under ASan+UBSan+LSan (must stay clean)
    just lint / format / doctor / clean

The green driver lives at ../../green/.agent/tmp/build/green (override GREEN).
`just baseline` (`c89-baseline.mk`) is NOT maintained; green + lint + the
Justfile recipes (including `just sanitize`) are the gates of record.

## Status

The v1 scope is implemented and green: the category kernel, orthogonal
capabilities, the concrete backends (finite/free/thin), the 1-categorical
algebra, the wrapper categories, universal structure (diagrams, cones,
limits/colimits, and the finite universal-construction finders), the exhaustive
law-family checkers, hardening (allocator/callback failure + sanitizer-clean),
and the ABI/architecture audit. Deferred to v2: adjunctions, monads,
monoidal/enriched settings, profunctors/presheaves, Kan extensions,
fibrations, higher categories, toposes, and model categories.
